  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Issue appeared with the release of VRChat 2023.3.1, aka Video on Quest and OSCQuery support update.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Have OSC enabled in either Radial menu -> Options -> OSC\n\nor in Main Menu -> Avatars -> OSC.\n\n2. Quit the game.\n\n3. Start it again.\n\n4. After you load in locomotion tunneling will be stuck on high setting, even though UI indicates otherwise.\n\nChanging that setting will have no effect.\n\nOn desktop mode I additionally noticed that mouse sensitivity is set to default 100%. More settings that I initially didn't notice might be also be affected in a similar way.\n\nThe only way to fix that is to turn OSC and restart.\n\nOther things I tried to debug this issue before I found out it was OSC was to clear local profile data from within game and clearing content of system registry key HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\SOFTWARE\\VRChat\\VRChat.\n\nAfter changing all of my settings to my usual ones (includes enabling OSC) caused issue to reappear after a restart.\n\nIssue happens in desktop and in VR.\n\nNot too sure if it happens consistently for everyone.",
